.TH SDL_HINT_RETURN_KEY_HIDES_IME 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_RETURN_KEY_HIDES_IME \- A variable to control whether the return key on the soft keyboard should hide the soft keyboard on Android and iOS.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_RETURN_KEY_HIDES_IME \(dqSDL_RETURN_KEY_HIDES_IME\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This hint sets the default value of
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_MULTILINE_BOOLEAN \[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: The return key will be handled as a key event\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: The return key will hide the keyboard\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

